claim.claim-text:
24. A transdermal iontopheresis method using the electrode assembly according to claim 21 which comprises: determining a set of desired criteria for delivery of a dmg using transdermal iontopheresis, the set of desired criteria selected from the group consisting of muscle and nerve tissue stimulation, depth of penetration, dmg delivery rate/magnitude, and maximum current density to avoid burning; 

 using relational criteria selected from the group of criteria relating i) AC frequency/pulse duration to nerve or muscle tissue stimulation, ii) maximum current density to skin buming, iii) ionic concentration to depth of penetration and AC frequency/pulse duration, and iv) aperture size or spacing to current density, determining transdermal iontopheresis operational criteria selected from the group consisting of AC frequency/pulse duration, current density, ionic concentration, aperture size or aperture spacing for achieving the set of desired criteria; and engaging in transdermal iontopheresis using the transdermal iontopheresis operational criteria. 25. A transdermal iontopheresis method which comprises: determining a set of desired criteria for delivery of a drug using transdermal iontopheresis, the set of desired criteria selected from the group consisting of muscle and nerve tissue stimulation, depth of penetration, drug delivery rate/magnitude, and maximum current density to avoid burning; using relational criteria selected from the group of criteria relating i) AC frequency/pulse duration to nerve or muscle tissue stimulation, ii) maximum current density to skin burning, iii) ionic concentration to depth of penetration and AC frequency/pulse duration, and iv) electrode size to current density, determining transdermal iontopheresis operational criteria selected from the group consisting of AC frequency/pulse duration, current density, ionic concentration and electrode size for achieving the set of desired criteria; and engaging in transdermal iontopheresis using the transdermal iontopheresis operational criteria. 26. A transdermal iontopheresis method for superficial skin which comprises: determining a set of desired criteria for delivery of a drug to the superficial skin using transdermal iontopheresis, the set of desired criteria selected from the group consisting of muscle and nerve tissue stimulation, low depth of penetration, drug delivery rate/magnitude, and maximum current density to avoid buming; 

 using relational criteria selected from the group of criteria relating i) AC frequency/pulse duration to nerve or muscle tissue stimulation, ii) maximum current density to skin burning, iii) ionic concentration to depth of penetration and AC frequency/pulse duration, and iv) electrode spacing, determining transdermal iontopheresis operational criteria selected from the group consisting of AC frequency/pulse duration, current density, ionic concentration and electrode spacing for achieving the set of desired criteria; and engaging in transdermal iontopheresis using the transdermal iontopheresis operational criteria.
